<h2>Asobi 1.0 (build 1232) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases on your iPad or iPhone, no links to type:</b> in the Showcase window, Pair iPad or iPhone… shows a code. Point the device's Camera at it and tap Open in Asobi, and the Asobi app's start screen lists this Mac's live showcases. When you make, edit, extend or end a showcase here, the list follows. The list is sealed with the code's key, so the relay can't read it. Make a New Pairing… shuts out the devices paired before. Also in the Review Manager.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1210) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Edit a showcase after posting it:</b> in the Review Manager, Edit… on a live showcase changes its title, the line under it, sign-in, Skip and the closing card's button and link. The link stays the same, nothing is sent again, and the session doesn't need to be open.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1202) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Reopening a showcase:</b> after a restart, reopening a live showcase from the Review Manager no longer leaves its window waiting on the email preview. The preview comes back, and Save GIF works again.</li>
<li><b>Review Manager:</b> each link now says how long it really works, with or without Asobi open.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1199) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases in more than one tab:</b> each tab now has its own Share and Showcase windows, so a new tab with a different clip can make its own showcase while another stays live.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1196) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Showcases on iPhone and iPad:</b> a showcase's sound now travels inside the picture, so it stays in sync on every device, through scrubs and full screen. On an iPhone, a one-clip showcase goes truly full screen. Remake a showcase to get it.</li>
<li><b>Skip sign-in on by default:</b> new showcases let viewers skip the name and email card. Turn it off in Make Showcase if you want every visitor signed in.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1178) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Save on quit works again:</b> choosing Save when Asobi asks about unsaved changes now saves and quits (or relaunches after an update). A session with a note attachment used to read as unsaved right after saving, so the quit was cancelled, and a session you had just saved asked again.</li>
<li><b>Quiet jumps:</b> clicking a note, its timecode or a marker no longer plays a repeating snatch of sound. Only dragging the playhead plays audio while stopped.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1174) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Reports, redesigned:</b> the notes report and the review activity report now use Asobi&#8217;s own design, like the manual: numbered entries, the notes in a readable serif with a byline each, replies under their notes, and nothing split across a page.</li>
<li><b>Spell check in comments:</b> notes and replies get the Mac&#8217;s red underline, with right-click suggestions. Autocorrect is there too if you want it: Settings ▸ Notes or Edit ▸ Spelling in Comments.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1170) <span class="when">Oct 3, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Timeline markers:</b> notes show as a blue line, markup as an amber triangle on the top edge, like a mark in an edit application. A frame with both shows both.</li>
<li><b>Replies:</b> a Send button appears beside a reply as you type (Return still sends).</li>
<li><b>Note report:</b> replies print under their notes, the comment text is larger, and small markup is shown magnified with the whole frame as an inset that stays clear of the marks.</li>
<li>Small fixes and improvements.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
